-+## Changed
-+
-+- Added `crates/features/run/src/feature/commit.rs`: a verified task in a
-+  worktree is committed with the task's scoped status paths, its untracked
-+  test files, and whichever of `.run/done/<task>`,
-+  `.run/results/<task>.md`, `.run/events/<task>.jsonl` and `tasks.md` exist.
-+  A refused commit leaves every file as it was and fails with
-+  `task <task> of <folder> is done, but osq could not commit it: <error>`.
-+- Added `crates/features/run/src/feature/message.rs`: TypeScript's pure commit
-+  message formatter, the `Osq-Change`/`Osq-Task`/`Osq-Model`/`Osq-Version`
-+  trailers from the last complete `started` event, the folder's numeric id,
-+  and whole elapsed seconds from the last `started` event, clamped at zero.
-+- Extended `scope.rs` with `commit_paths` so the scope audit and the commit
-+  share one source for scope coverage, lock rules and language test folders.
-+- `run.rs` commits after the done record only when git is on and the change
-+  lives in a worktree; a change in the checkout makes no commit.
-+- `worktree.rs` gained `is_worktree`, comparing canonicalized roots.
-+- `start.rs` now records the crate version as `osqVersion`, so the verified
-+  commit's trailers match TypeScript's.
-+- `text.rs` gained the failed-commit message.
-+- Added `tests/run_worktree.rs`, proving "Verified task commit", "Verified
-+  task commit fails" and "Trailers from the last started event", plus path
-+  selection, elapsed-time clamping, and no commit for a checkout change.
-+- Extended `tests/worktree_support/mod.rs` with the executor model, an
-+  executable refusing-hook case, and an approval commit that includes the
-+  seal so the records can be committed.
-+
-+## Deviated
-+
-+- The worktree test repository removes the fixture's `.gitignore`, whose
-+  `.run/` rule made `git add` refuse the done, result and event records. The
-+  approval commit now adds and commits the seal instead of using
-+  `--allow-empty`.
-+- `start.rs` sets `osqVersion` where task 2 left it absent, because the
-+  required trailer must come from the run's own `started` event.
-+
-+## Missing context
-+
-+- Task 2's note said the fixture `.gitignore` forced `--allow-empty`; task 3
-+  needed those ignored records in the commit, so the support repository drops
-+  that ignore rule. The delta does not say which takes precedence.
-+
-+## Next
-+
-+None.
